cff-version: "1.2.0"
message: >-
  If you use Fruth, its software design, or its evaluation artifacts in research
  or a published system, please cite this software and identify the exact version
  and commit or local snapshot used. Fruth 0.1.2 derives
  from Ollmo 0.1.1 (https://github.com/fl0ri0/ollmo). Its version identifies
  the Fruth software, while Ollmo 0.1.1 identifies the source baseline.
title: "Fruth"
authors:
  - name: "fl0ri0"
type: software
version: "0.1.2"
date-released: "2026-09-19"
repository-code: "https://github.com/fl0ri0/fruth"
abstract: >-
  Fruth is a durable semantic state inference engine for local AI. A response
  develops through a fluid possibility space: intent is interpreted into candidate
  work graphs, and relevant candidates become obligations through validated
  promotion. Semantic depth and structural granularity guide interpretation,
  decomposition, and review. Late fill continues already-promoted obligations and
  binds later materialized results and their evidence back into the same response.
  Work advances through execution, evidence-gated
  closure review, and intent-preserving block resolution. Freezing records the
  evidenced current state, including unresolved work. Reviewed learning can inform
  future proposals; subsequent continuation, bounded repair, and reviewed graph
  rebase preserve earlier frozen evidence through explicit successor lineage.
  Interpretive inference proposes, while runtime contracts govern accepted
  transitions and execution.
license: "Apache-2.0"
